From dfc98789aa0c61a7ed92c596588b569ea56553e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:30:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fips): load registered FIPS provider

Discover the Azure Linux FIPS provider from a package-owned registration
file instead of hard-coding SymCrypt. Activate it before ambient providers
and merge its fetch properties in kernel FIPS mode.

Require exactly one .cnf registration under
/etc/pki/tls/azl-openssl-fips-provider.d. Its [azl_fips_provider] section
identifies the provider and configuration section and supplies the default
properties to merge. Provider packages own these registrations and must be
mutually exclusive.

Fail closed for missing, ambiguous, malformed, or inactive registrations,
and prevent fallback activation after initialization failure. Cover
discovery, validation, repeated loads, library-context isolation, and the
real initialization path.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
